WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.805
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.979
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:14.601
Unit thirteen: Transportation. Today you will explain how you travel and give reasons.

4
00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.472
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.433 --> 00:00:21.933
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:23.622
Commute.

7
00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:27.650
Commute means to travel to school or work regularly.

8
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.261
I commute by bus every day.

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.177
Your turn. Say: Commute.

10
00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:36.779
Commute.

11
00:00:37.517 --> 00:00:38.564
Rush hour.

12
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.664
Rush hour means the busy time when everyone travels.

13
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.122
The roads are full at rush hour.

14
00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:48.961
Your turn. Say: Rush hour.

15
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:52.952
Rush hour.

16
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:54.532
Fare.

17
00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:57.656
Fare means the money you pay for a trip.

18
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.087
The bus fare is very cheap.

19
00:01:00.683 --> 00:01:02.906
Your turn. Say: Fare.

20
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:06.594
Fare.

21
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.165
Route.

22
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.113
Route means the way you travel from one place to another.

23
00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:14.403
This route avoids the traffic.

24
00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:16.880
Your turn. Say: Route.

25
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:20.467
Route.

26
00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:22.612
Punctuality.

27
00:01:23.617 --> 00:01:25.744
Punctuality means being on time.

28
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.988
Punctuality is important for buses.

29
00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:32.549
Your turn. Say: Punctuality.

30
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.610
Punctuality.

31
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.281
Carpool.

32
00:01:39.283 --> 00:01:42.409
Carpool means to share a car with others going the same way.

33
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:45.585
Three families carpool to school.

34
00:01:46.183 --> 00:01:48.627
Your turn. Say: Carpool.

35
00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:52.433
Carpool.

36
00:01:53.183 --> 00:01:54.219
Pedestrian.

37
00:01:55.217 --> 00:01:57.843
Pedestrian means a person walking in the street.

38
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.879
Drivers must stop for pedestrians.

39
00:02:01.483 --> 00:02:04.205
Your turn. Say: Pedestrian.

40
00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.010
Pedestrian.

41
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:09.890
Traffic jam.

42
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:14.055
Traffic jam means a long line of cars that can't move.

43
00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.650
We were stuck in a traffic jam.

44
00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.809
Your turn. Say: Traffic jam.

45
00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:23.958
Traffic jam.

46
00:02:24.717 --> 00:02:25.428
Delay.

47
00:02:26.417 --> 00:02:28.683
Delay means a time when something is late.

48
00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:31.178
There's a delay because of the rain.

49
00:02:31.783 --> 00:02:34.273
Your turn. Say: Delay.

50
00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:37.821
Delay.

51
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:39.503
Vehicle.

52
00:02:40.517 --> 00:02:44.362
Vehicle means a machine for carrying people, like a car or bus.

53
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.717
Electric vehicles are quiet.

54
00:02:47.317 --> 00:02:49.725
Your turn. Say: Vehicle.

55
00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:53.591
Vehicle.

56
00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:55.456
Sustainable.

57
00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:59.564
Sustainable means not harming the planet for the future.

58
00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.602
Cycling is a sustainable way to travel.

59
00:03:03.217 --> 00:03:05.660
Your turn. Say: Sustainable.

60
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.524
Sustainable.

61
00:03:10.283 --> 00:03:11.342
Eco-friendly.

62
00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:15.325
Eco-friendly means good for the environment.

63
00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:18.172
Buses are more eco-friendly than cars.

64
00:03:18.783 --> 00:03:21.714
Your turn. Say: Eco-friendly.

65
00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:25.928
Eco-friendly.

66
00:03:26.733 --> 00:03:30.291
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:33.231
Visal, how do you get to school?

68
00:03:34.317 --> 00:03:37.036
I take the city bus because the fare is cheap.

69
00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.848
Why not go by car?

70
00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:46.006
Because there are traffic jams at rush hour. The bus has its own route.

71
00:03:47.117 --> 00:03:48.745
Is the bus punctual?

72
00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:53.478
Usually. I like it because it's eco-friendly too.

73
00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:56.343
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:57.183 --> 00:03:59.775
Grammar focus: Reasons with because.

75
00:04:00.075 --> 00:04:01.297
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:01.983 --> 00:04:04.238
I carpool because it is eco-friendly.

77
00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.579
I cycle because it's good exercise.

78
00:04:08.483 --> 00:04:10.669
We were late because of the traffic jam.

79
00:04:11.633 --> 00:04:15.107
'because' + a full sentence; 'because of' + a noun.

80
00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:19.872
Be careful! Don't say: I was late because the traffic jam.

81
00:04:21.833 --> 00:04:24.088
Say: I was late because of the traffic jam.

82
00:04:24.388 --> 00:04:26.341
Use 'because of' before a noun.

83
00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:30.343
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.587
Getting Around the City.

85
00:04:32.887 --> 00:04:36.547
During rush hour, traffic jams cause long delays in Phnom Penh.

86
00:04:37.533 --> 00:04:40.415
Many people use motorbikes because they are fast.

87
00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.350
I take the city bus because the fare is cheap and the route is easy.

88
00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:49.829
My neighbors carpool because it is eco-friendly and saves money.

89
00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:55.329
If more people choose sustainable transport, the air will be cleaner.

90
00:04:56.433 --> 00:05:00.238
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:01.083 --> 00:05:03.269
I walk to school blank it's close.

92
00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:07.060
A, because. B, because of. C, so.

93
00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.402
The answer is A: because.

94
00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:15.550
The money you pay for a trip is the blank.

95
00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:18.957
A, fare. B, route. C, delay.

96
00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.534
The answer is A: fare.

97
00:05:25.683 --> 00:05:28.031
A person walking in the street is a blank.

98
00:05:28.331 --> 00:05:31.961
A, pedestrian. B, vehicle. C, driver.

99
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.813
The answer is A: pedestrian.

100
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.943
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:42.783 --> 00:05:45.003
How do you usually get to school, and why?

102
00:05:53.817 --> 00:05:55.456
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:55.756 --> 00:06:03.192
I usually ride my bicycle to school because it's close, and it's eco-friendly. I also avoid the traffic jams.

104
00:06:03.492 --> 00:06:05.062
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:10.181
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and reasons with because.

106
00:06:10.481 --> 00:06:15.200
Today's value is protecting nature. Keep the sea, rivers and forests clean.

107
00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.118
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:18.418 --> 00:06:21.012
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

